    "result_text": "All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the derived read-only `ownerSegment` field to the owner response, formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`, reusing the existing membership-level and locality derivations rather than recomputing them.\n\nEach piece landed in the class that owns that responsibility:\n\n- **`util/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 an enum of the four segments with `of(membershipLevel, locality)` composing TIER (`PREMIUM` when membership level \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`) and AREA (`METRO` for a known region, else `REGIONAL`). Mirrors the existing `AgeBand`/`ContactPreference` enum-util style.\n- **`util/CityRegion.java`** \u2014 added a small `isKnown(String region)` predicate (a region that is neither `null` nor `UNKNOWN`), since `CityRegion` already owns the `UNKNOWN` sentinel. This is what \"known region (NSW/VIC/QLD)\" means.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 a new `ownerSegment(owner)` mapping method that feeds the already-computed `membershipLevel(owner)` and `locality(owner)` into `OwnerSegment.of(...)`, converting to the generated `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum`. No logic duplicated \u2014 it composes the existing derivations.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `ownerSegment` string enum property (read-only, four values) so the generated DTO carries the field and its `OwnerSegmentEnum`.\n\nThe two new `AcceptanceTest` cases (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known NSW city, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown-region city) both pass, and the full suite is green.",
